AB  - Cyber-physical systems (CPS) integrated with cloud platforms are central to real-time data processing and automation, driving advancements in sectors like e-healthcare, autonomous vehicle systems, smart cities, and industrial automation. However, the increasing reliance on centralized cloud infrastructures introduces significant challenges related to data privacy, system integrity, and digital sovereignty. Implementing robust security measures, such as encryption and access control, is crucial to protect sensitive data, maintain system reliability, and assert control over digital assets, aligning with the growing emphasis on trust, autonomy, and data sovereignty in distributed systems. Ciphertext-Policy Attribute-Based Encryption (CP-ABE) is a promising public key encryption technique enabling fine-grained access control while ensuring data confidentiality. However, traditional CP-ABE schemes suffer from high computational overhead and latency, limiting their effectiveness in resource-constrained and real-time CPS settings. To address these limitations, we propose a lightweight, pairing-free CP-ABE cryptosystem utilizing elliptic curve point multiplications for enhanced performance. By offloading complex encryption tasks to fog nodes, our approach reduces latency, decentralizes data management, and enhances digital sovereignty, ensuring compliance with data protection laws and mitigating risks associated with cross-border data transfers. Additionally, the system features multiple fog-based attribute authorities that manage disjoint sets of attributes, ensuring efficient key management and supporting user and attribute revocation without incurring additional overhead. Our decentralized approach strengthens trust, autonomy, and resilience in CPS, making it suitable for dynamic, regulatory-compliant environments. Theoretical analysis and performance evaluations demonstrate the scalability and security of our cryptosystem, offering a robust solution that addresses the challenges of pairing-free CP-ABE and promotes digital sovereignty in CPS environments.
