DO  - https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-443-27692-7.00008-3
UR  - https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/B9780443276927000083
KW  - Security and privacy
KW  - Digital twin
KW  - Smart healthcare
KW  - Ethical governance
KW  - Metaverse
KW  - Virtual reality
KW  - Augmented reality
AB  - This chapter reviews the intersection of artificial intelligence (AI) and metaverse technologies in transforming smart healthcare delivery, while critically analyzing the security and privacy frameworks necessary for safe adoption. The integration of AI with immersive environments such as virtual reality and augmented reality enhances diagnostics, medical training, telemedicine, and patient care through personalization, real-time analytics, and predictive insights. However, these benefits are counterbalanced by significant risks, including adversarial attacks on AI models, data poisoning, identity theft, deepfake exploitation, and unauthorized access to sensitive biometric and behavioral data. Privacy challenges intensify due to continuous data collection in immersive environments, raising issues around informed consent, data sovereignty, and compliance with regulations such as the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act, the General Data Protection Regulation, and ISO/IEC 27701. Furthermore, governance gaps surrounding liability, interoperability, accessibility, and digital equity are examined, emphasizing the need for cross-disciplinary collaboration and policy reform. Future directions include the integration of explainable AI, digital twins, federated systems, and secure edge computing to advance personalized, secure, and equitable healthcare ecosystems. Ultimately, the chapter underscores that security, privacy, and ethical governance are foundational for realizing AI-enabled metaverse healthcare.
